{
  "description": "issue #676 (SP4): `each <block>` runs its block ONCE per turtle in the current `tell` set, in insertion order. With `tell [ :a :b ]` the block runs for :a (id 1) then :b (id 2); inside each run `who` reports that turtle (`who == :a` is `true` on :a's run, `false` on :b's) and its `forward`/`right` events carry that turtle's `turtle_id`. Every change of the addressed set — here from `each`/`tell` — also emits the addressing `primitive` event carrying `addressing: { addressed_turtle_ids, current_turtle_id }`, so a consumer can identify the addressed turtle set (issue #766, spec/rendering.md:191); `ask`/`each` emit one again when the previous set is restored, on every exit path.",
